<title>USA: Poland to launch $300 mln yankee bond this week.</title>
<headline>Poland to launch $300 mln yankee bond this week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Poland will sell $300 million in seven-year yankee bonds later this week, market sources said Monday.</p>
<p>The bonds are expected to be rated at Poland's sovereign ceiling, BBB-minus by Standard and Poor's and Baa3 by Moody's Investors Service, the source said.</p>
<p>J.P. Morgan is acting as lead manager to the deal.</p>
<p>(( N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1671))</p>
